 "name": "SD: A vaccination clinic's doses: the truth",
 "description": "Tests co-flows on a stock that also drains: every vaccination uses a dose, both of booked patients from the waiting list and of walk-ins who come straight from outside, while doses also expire; the vaccinations and the expiry share what the fridge holds. Doses come once a week, so late in a busy week they run out and the waiting list grows. A second nurse (an announced era) doubles how fast the waiting list is seen.",
